h **leave-one-participant-out** outer validation; every imputation, scaling and hyper-parameter\nchoice is made inside the training fold. The same participants are used for A and B, so their errors are paired.\nInference: paired participant bootstrap of ΔMAE, Wilcoxon signed-rank test, and a permutation test that shuffles the\nrecovery features across participants (repeating the full nested procedure each time).","metadata":{}},{"id":"11edfd3d","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 16 · RQ2 nested LOSO prediction with three learners ────────────────────\nFEAT_A = [\"perf_WB\", \"perf_S1\", \"R_comp\"]\nFEAT_B = FEAT_A + [\"RB_comp\", \"slope_comp\"]\nREC_IDX = [FEAT_B.index(\"RB_comp\"), FEAT_B.index(\"slope_comp\")]\n\n\ndef make_ridge():\n    return Pipeline([(\"imp\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")), (\"sc\", StandardScaler()),\n                     (\"m\", RidgeCV(alphas=np.array(cfg.ridge_alphas)))])\n\n\ndef make_enet():\n    return Pipeline([(\"imp\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")), (\"sc\", StandardScaler()),\n                     (\"m\", ElasticNetCV(alphas=np.array(cfg.enet_alphas), l1_ratio=list(cfg.enet_l1_ratios),\n                                        cv=KFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=cfg.seed), max_iter=100_000))])\n\n\ndef make_gbr():\n    return GridSearchCV(GradientBoostingRegressor(random_state=cfg.seed), cfg.gbr_grid,\n                        cv=KFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=cfg.seed), scoring=\"neg_mean_absolute_error\",\n                        n_jobs=cfg.n_jobs)\n\n\nLEARNERS = {\"Ridge\": make_ridge, \"Elastic net\": make_enet}\nif cfg.rq2_run_gbr:\n    LEARNERS[\"Gradient boosting\"] = make_gbr\n\n\ndef loso_predict(X: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray, factory) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    n = len(y)\n    pred, train_mean = np.empty(n), np.empty(n)\n    for i in range(n):\n        tr = np.arange(n) != i\n        model = factory()\n        model.fit(X[tr], y[tr])\n        pred[i] = float(np.ravel(model.predict(X[i:i + 1]))[0])\n        train_mean[i] = y[tr].mean()\n    return pred, train_mean\n\n\ndef reg_metrics(y, pred, train_mean) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    e = y - pred\n    return {\"MAE\": float(np.mean(np.abs(e))), \"RMSE\": float(np.sqrt(np.mean(e ** 2))),\n            \"R2_oos\": float(1 - np.sum(e ** 2) / np.sum((y - train_mean) ** 2))}\n\n\nD2 = PART[[\"subject\", \"perf_S2\"] + FEAT_B].dropna(subset=[\"perf_S2\", \"perf_WB\", \"perf_S1\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\nD2 = D2.dropna(subset=[\"R_comp\", \"RB_comp\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\nY2 = D2[\"perf_S2\"].to_numpy(float)\nXA, XB = D2[FEAT_A].to_numpy(float), D2[FEAT_B].to_numpy(float)\nRQ2_PRED, rq2_rows = {}, []\nif len(D2) >= 12:\n    with Timer(f\"RQ2 nested LOSO (n = {len(D2)})\"):\n        for lname, factory in LEARNERS.items():\n            pa, ma = loso_predict(XA, Y2, factory)\n            pb, mb = loso_predict(XB, Y2, factory)\n            RQ2_PRED[lname] = {\"A\": pa, \"B\": pb, \"trainmean\": ma}\n            mA, mB = reg_metrics(Y2, pa, ma), reg_metrics(Y2, pb, mb)\n            ea, eb = np.abs(Y2 - pa), np.abs(Y2 - pb)\n            rng = rng_for(f\"rq2_boot_{lname}\")\n            bd = np.empty(cfg.n_boot)\n            for b in range(cfg.n_boot):\n                idx = rng.integers(0, len(Y2), len(Y2))\n                bd[b] = ea[idx].mean() - eb[idx].mean()\n            lo, hi = pct_ci(bd)\n            wil = stats.wilcoxon(ea, eb) if np.any(ea != eb) else None\n            rq2_rows.append({\"learner\": lname, \"n\": len(Y2),\n                             \"MAE_A\": mA[\"MAE\"], \"MAE_B\": mB[\"MAE\"], \"RMSE_A\": mA[\"RMSE\"], \"RMSE_B\": mB[\"RMSE\"],\n                             \"R2oos_A\": mA[\"R2_oos\"], \"R2oos_B\": mB[\"R2_oos\"],\n                             \"dMAE_A_minus_B\": mA[\"MAE\"] - mB[\"MAE\"], \"dMAE_ci_low\": lo, \"dMAE_ci_high\": hi,\n                             \"wilcoxon_p\": float(wil.pvalue) if wil is not None else np.nan})\n    RQ2_TABLE = pd.DataFrame(rq2_rows)\n    save_table(RQ2_TABLE, \"rq2_prediction\")\n    print(RQ2_TABLE.round(3).to_string(index=False))\nelse:\n    RQ2_TABLE = pd.DataFrame()\n    LOG.error(f\"RQ2 skipped: only {len(D2)} complete participants\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-12T18:20:55.500931Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-12T18:20:55.501465Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-12T18:34:25.038813Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-12T18:20:55.501441Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-12T18:34:25.038179Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"18:20:55 | INFO    | ▶ RQ2 nested LOSO (n = 35)\n18:34:25 | INFO    | ■ RQ2 nested LOSO (n = 35) — 809.5 s\n18:34:25 | INFO    | table → rq2_prediction.csv (3 rows)\n          learner  n   MAE_A   MAE_B  RMSE_A  RMSE_B  R2oos_A  R2oos_B  dMAE_A_minus_B  dMAE_ci_low  dMAE_ci_high  wilcoxon_p\n            Ridge 35 219.611 234.676 293.731 309.625    0.698    0.665         -15.065      -22.431        -8.763       0.000\n      Elastic net 35 210.237 213.116 279.492 281.432    0.727    0.723          -2.879       -8.736         2.946       0.098\nGradient boosting 35 220.676 209.482 307.149 279.251    0.670    0.727          11.194      -27.237        48.107       0.576\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":17},{"id":"73b351cd","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 17 · RQ2 permutation test (Ridge, full nested refit) and Figure 4 ──────\nif \"Ridge\" in RQ2_PRED:\n    mae_a = float(np.mean(np.abs(Y2 - RQ2_PRED[\"Ridge\"][\"A\"])))\n    obs = mae_a - float(np.mean(np.abs(Y2 - RQ2_PRED[\"Ridge\"][\"B\"])))\n\n    def _perm(seed: int) -> float:\n        r = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n        Xp = XB.copy()\n        Xp[:, REC_IDX] = XB[r.permutation(len(Y2))][:, REC_IDX]\n        pb, _ = loso_predict(Xp, Y2, make_ridge)\n        return mae_a - float(np.mean(np.abs(Y2 - pb)))\n\n    with Timer(f\"RQ2 permutation test ({cfg.n_perm} permutations)\"):\n        seeds = rng_for(\"rq2_perm\").integers(0, 2 ** 31 - 1, cfg.n_perm)\n        NULL = np.array(Parallel(n_jobs=cfg.n_jobs)(delayed(_perm)(int(s)) for s in seeds))\n    p_perm = (1 + np.sum(NULL >= obs)) / (1 + NULL.size)\n    RESULTS[\"RQ2\"] = {\"table\": RQ2_TABLE.to_dict(orient=\"records\"), \"ridge_dMAE\": obs,\n                      \"ridge_permutation_p_one_sided\": float(p_perm), \"n_perm\": int(NULL.size)}\n    LOG.info(f\"RQ2 Ridge: ΔMAE (A − B) = {obs:.2f} fuel units; permutation p = {p_perm:.4f} (one-sided, B better)\")\n\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(COL2, 2.6), layout=\"constrained\")\n    gs = fig.add_gridspec(1, 3)\n    ax1, ax2, ax3 = (fig.add_subplot(gs[0, i]) for i in range(3))\n    pa, pb = RQ2_PRED[\"Ridge\"][\"A\"], RQ2_PRED[\"Ridge\"][\"B\"]\n    lim = [min(Y2.min(), pa.min(), pb.min()) * 0.95, max(Y2.max(), pa.max(), pb.max()) * 1.05]\n    ax1.plot(lim, lim, color=\"#777777\", lw=0.6, ls=(0, (3, 2)))\n    ax1.scatter(Y2, pa, s=11, marker=\"o\", facecolor=\"none\", edgecolor=OI[\"grey\"], lw=0.7, label=\"A: conventional\")\n    ax1.scatter(Y2, pb, s=11, marker=\"o\", color=OI[\"blue\"], lw=0, alpha=0.85, label=\"B: + recovery\")\n    ax1.set_xlim(lim)\n    ax1.set_ylim(lim)\n    ax1.set_xlabel(\"Observed Stress-2 error\")\n    ax1.set_ylabel(\"LOSO-predicted error\")\n    ax1.legend(loc=\"upper left\", handletextpad=0.2)\n    ax1.set_title(\"Ridge, held-out predictions\", loc=\"left\")\n    ea, eb = np.abs(Y2 - pa), np.abs(Y2 - pb)\n    order = np.argsort(ea - eb)\n    for k, i in enumerate(order):\n        better = eb[i] < ea[i]\n        ax2.plot([0, 1], [ea[i], eb[i]], color=OI[\"blue\"] if better else OI[\"vermillion\"], lw=0.5, alpha=0.7)\n    ax2.set_xticks([0, 1], [\"Model A\", \"Model B\"])\n    ax2.set_xlim(-0.25, 1.25)\n    ax2.set_ylabel(\"Absolute prediction error\")\n    ax2.set_title(f\"Paired errors ({int((eb < ea).sum())}/{len(ea)} improved)\", loc=\"left\")\n    counts, _, _ = ax3.hist(NULL, bins=30, color=\"#BDBDBD\", edgecolor=\"white\", lw=0.3)\n    ax3.axvline(obs, color=OI[\"vermillion\"], lw=1.2)\n    ax3.set_ylim(0, counts.max() * 1.35)                    # headroom for the annotation\n    ax3.set_xlabel(\"ΔMAE (A − B) under permutation\")\n    ax3.set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n    ax3.text(0.03, 0.97, f\"observed ΔMAE = {obs:.1f}\\n{fmt_p(p_perm)} ({NULL.size} perm.)\", transform=ax3.transAxes,\n             ha=\"left\", va=\"top\", fontsize=6.3)\n    ax3.set_title(\"Permutation null\", loc=\"left\")\n    label_panels(fig, (ax1, ax2, ax3))\n    save_fig(fig, \"fig4_rq2_out_of_sample_prediction\",\n             \"Figure 4. RQ2. (a) Leave-one-participant-out predictions of Stress-2 RESMAN error from the conventional (A) and \"\n             \"recovery-aware (B) ridge models. (b) Paired absolute errors (blue: B better; orange: A better). \"\n             f\"(c) Null distribution of ΔMAE from {NULL.size} permutations of the recovery features; vertical line = observed.\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"98298f67","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## RQ3 — How portable are physiological stressor signatures across contexts?\n| Dataset | Control (0) | Stressor (1) | Signals used |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| PhysioNet | Working Baseline | Stress 1 + Stress 2 | E4 wrist EDA + BVP (same pipeline as WESAD) |\n| WESAD | Baseline | TSST stress | E4 wrist EDA + BVP |\n| SWELL-KW | Neutral work | Time pressure + interruptions | Pre-computed HR / RMSSD (/ SCL if present) |\n\n**Calibration without label leakage.** For every participant, the first *k* control windows (k = 2) are reserved\nas a personal baseline and are **removed from every test set in both settings**, so calibrated and uncalibrated\nmodels are scored on identical windows. Calibrated features are baseline-relative (log-ratios), which makes devices\nand electrode sites with different absolute units comparable. Stress-period labels of the target are never used.\nPositive class = *experimental stressor condition*, not a validated measure of perceived stress.","metadata":{}},{"id":"31199835","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 18 · WESAD wrist data → 60-s windows ───────────────────────────────────\nWESAD_FS = {\"BVP\": 64.0, \"EDA\": 4.0, \"ACC\": 32.0, \"label\": 700.0}\nWESAD_LABELS = {1: 0, 2: 1}          # 1 = baseline → control, 2 = stress → stressor; others excluded\n\n\ndef label_runs(lab: np.ndarray, fs: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    lab = np.asarray(lab).ravel()\n    change = np.flatnonzero(np.diff(lab)) + 1\n    starts, ends = np.r_[0, change], np.r_[change, lab.size]\n    return np.column_stack([lab[starts], starts / fs, ends / fs]).astype(float)\n\n\ndef load_wesad_subject(pkl: Path) -> Dict[str, np.ndarray]:\n    cache = CACHE_DIR / \"wesad\" / f\"{pkl.stem}.npz\"\n    if cache.is_file():\n        with np.load(cache) as z:\n            return {k: z[k] for k in z.files}\n    with open(pkl, \"rb\") as fh:\n        d = pickle.load(fh, encoding=\"latin1\")\n    wrist = d[\"signal\"][\"wrist\"]\n    out = {\"eda\": np.asarray(wrist[\"EDA\"], float).ravel(), \"bvp\": np.asarray(wrist[\"BVP\"], float).ravel(),\n           \"acc\": np.asarray(wrist[\"ACC\"], float), \"runs\": label_runs(d[\"label\"], WESAD_FS[\"label\"])}\n    del d, wrist\n    gc.collect()\n    cache.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    np.savez_compressed(cache, **out)\n    return out\n\n\ndef windows_from_runs(runs: np.ndarray, label_map: Dict[int, int]) -> List[Tuple[int, float, float]]:\n    wins = []\n    for lab, a, b in runs:\n        if int(lab) not in label_map:\n            continue\n        t = a + cfg.transition_s\n        while t + cfg.window_s <= b + 1e-9:\n            wins.append((label_map[int(lab)], t, t + cfg.window_s))\n            t += cfg.window_s\n    return wins\n\n\ndef mark_calibration(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    df = df.sort_values([\"subject\", \"t0\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n    df[\"is_cal\"] = False\n    ctrl = df[df[\"label\"] == 0]\n    cal_idx = ctrl.groupby(\"subject\", sort=False).head(cfg.n_cal_windows).index\n    df.loc[cal_idx, \"is_cal\"] = True\n    return df\n\n\nWIN = {}\nif WESAD_PKLS:\n    rows = []\n    with Timer(f\"WESAD feature extraction ({len(WESAD_PKLS)} subjects)\"):\n        for pkl in WESAD_PKLS:\n            try:\n                w = load_wesad_subject(pkl)\n                sig = build_signals(\"WESAD\", pkl.stem, w[\"eda\"], WESAD_FS[\"EDA\"], 0.0, w[\"bvp\"], WESAD_FS[\"BVP\"], 0.0,\n                                    w[\"acc\"], WESAD_FS[\"ACC\"], 0.0)\n                for lab, t0, t1 in windows_from_runs(w[\"runs\"], WESAD_LABELS):\n                    rows.append({\"dataset\": \"WESAD\", \"subject\": pkl.stem, \"label\": lab, \"t0\": t0,\n                                 **window_features(sig, t0, t1)})\n            except Exception as exc:\n                LOG.warning(f\"WESAD {pkl.stem} excluded — {exc}\")\n    if rows:\n        WIN[\"WESAD\"] = mark_calibration(pd.DataFrame(rows))","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"72b16c71","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 19 · SWELL-KW pre-computed features → harmonised windows ───────────────\nSWELL_COND = {\"no stress\": 0, \"nostress\": 0, \"neutral\": 0, \"n\": 0,\n              \"time pressure\": 1, \"timepressure\": 1, \"t\": 1, \"interruption\": 1, \"interruptions\": 1, \"i\": 1}\nSUBJECT_CANDIDATES = (\"subject\", \"subject_id\", \"subjectid\", \"participant\", \"participant_id\", \"pp\", \"user\",\n                      \"datasetid\")\nSWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS = False\n\n\ndef load_swell(paths: List[Path]) -> Optional[pd.DataFrame]:\n    global SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS\n    groups: Dict[Tuple[str, ...], List[pd.DataFrame]] = {}\n    for p in paths:\n        d = pd.read_csv(p, low_memory=False)\n        d.columns = [str(c).strip() for c in d.columns]\n        groups.setdefault(tuple(sorted(c.lower() for c in d.columns)), []).append(d)\n    if not groups:\n        return None\n    raw = pd.concat(max(groups.values(), key=lambda g: sum(len(x) for x in g)), ignore_index=True)\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in raw.columns}\n    cond = raw[cols[\"condition\"]].map(lambda v: re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", str(v).strip().lower().replace(\"_\", \" \")))\n    out = pd.DataFrame({\"dataset\": \"SWELL\", \"label\": cond.map(SWELL_COND)})\n    subj_col = None\n    for c in SUBJECT_CANDIDATES:\n        if c in cols and 10 <= raw[cols[c]].nunique() <= 60:\n            subj_col = cols[c]\n            break\n    SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS = subj_col is not None\n    out[\"subject\"] = (raw[subj_col].astype(str).radd(\"swell_\") if SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS\n                      else pd.Series([f\"row{i}\" for i in range(len(raw))]))\n    order_col = next((cols[c] for c in (\"timestamp\", \"time\", \"window\", \"blok\", \"block\", \"order\") if c in cols), None)\n    out[\"t0\"] = (pd.to_numeric(raw[order_col], errors=\"coerce\") if order_col is not None\n                 else pd.Series(np.arange(len(raw), dtype=float)))\n    if \"hr\" in cols:\n        out[\"hr_mean\"] = pd.to_numeric(raw[cols[\"hr\"]], errors=\"coerce\")\n    if \"rmssd\" in cols:\n        r = pd.to_numeric(raw[cols[\"rmssd\"]], errors=\"coerce\")\n        out[\"rmssd_ms\"] = r * 1000.0 if np.nanmedian(r) < 1.0 else r           # seconds → ms if needed\n    if \"scl\" in cols:\n        out[\"eda_tonic_mean\"] = pd.to_numeric(raw[cols[\"scl\"]], errors=\"coerce\")\n    out = out.dropna(subset=[\"label\"]).copy()\n    out[\"label\"] = out[\"label\"].astype(int)\n    if SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS:                                                    # cap heavily overlapping windows\n        # shuffle-then-head keeps grouping columns on every pandas version (groupby.apply drops them in pandas ≥ 3)\n        out = (out.sample(frac=1.0, random_state=cfg.seed)\n               .groupby([\"subject\", \"label\"], sort=False).head(cfg.swell_max_rows_per_cell))\n    else:\n        out = out.sample(min(len(out), 25 * 3 * cfg.swell_max_rows_per_cell), random_state=cfg.seed)\n        LOG.warning(\"SWELL-KW: no participant identifier found. Within-SWELL CV becomes row-level (optimistic, \"\n                    \"overlapping windows) and the calibrated setting is skipped for SWELL. Interpret with caution.\")\n    for f in FEATURE_POOL:\n        if f not in out:\n            out[f] = np.nan\n    return out.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n\nif SWELL_CSVS:\n    try:\n        sw = load_swell(SWELL_CSVS)\n        if sw is not None and sw[\"label\"].nunique() == 2:\n            WIN[\"SWELL\"] = mark_calibration(sw) if SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS else sw.assign(is_cal=False)\n            LOG.info(f\"SWELL-KW: {len(sw)} windows, subjects identified = {SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS}\")\n    except Exception as exc:\n        LOG.warning(f\"SWELL-KW could not be harmonised — {exc}\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"dac9176b","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 20 · PhysioNet windows, feature harmonisation and personal-baseline calibration ──\npn_rows = []\nfor sid, sig in PN_SIGNALS.items():\n    for ph, lab in ((\"WB\", 0), (\"S1\", 1), (\"S2\", 1)):\n        lo, hi = PHASE_BOUNDS[ph]\n        t = lo + cfg.transition_s\n        while t + cfg.window_s <= hi + 1e-9:\n            pn_rows.append({\"dataset\": \"PhysioNet\", \"subject\": sid, \"label\": lab, \"phase\": ph, \"t0\": t,\n                            **window_features(sig, t, t + cfg.window_s)})\n            t += cfg.window_s\nif pn_rows:\n    WIN = {\"PhysioNet\": mark_calibration(pd.DataFrame(pn_rows)), **WIN}\n\nLOGRATIO_EPS = {\"hr_mean\": 0.0, \"hr_std\": 0.1, \"rmssd_ms\": 1.0, \"eda_tonic_mean\": 0.01, \"scr_rate\": 0.5}\n\n\ndef calibrate(df: pd.DataFrame, feats: List[str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Baseline-relative features from the participant's reserved calibration windows only.\"\"\"\n    out = df.copy()\n    for subj, g in df.groupby(\"subject\", sort=False):\n        cal = g[g[\"is_cal\"]]\n        for f in feats:\n            if f == \"eda_tonic_slope\":\n                base = np.nanmedian(cal[\"eda_tonic_mean\"]) if cal[\"eda_tonic_mean\"].notna().any() else np.nan\n                out.loc[g.index, f] = g[f] / (abs(base) + 0.01)\n            else:\n                eps = LOGRATIO_EPS[f]\n                base = np.nanmedian(cal[f]) if cal[f].notna().any() else np.nan\n                with np.errstate(invalid=\"ignore\", divide=\"ignore\"):\n                    out.loc[g.index, f] = np.log((g[f].clip(lower=0) + eps) / (base + eps)) if base + eps > 0 else np.nan\n    return out\n\n\ndef available_features(df: pd.DataFrame) -> List[str]:\n    ev = df[~df[\"is_cal\"]]\n    return [f for f in FEATURE_POOL if f in ev and ev[f].notna().mean() >= cfg.feature_min_availability]\n\n\nAVAIL = {name: available_features(df) for name, df in WIN.items()}\nCAN_CAL = {name: (name != \"SWELL\" or SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS) for name in WIN}\nWIN_CAL = {name: calibrate(df, AVAIL[name]) for name, df in WIN.items() if CAN_CAL[name]}\nharm = pd.DataFrame([{\"dataset\": n, \"participants\": df[\"subject\"].nunique(), \"windows\": len(df),\n                      \"control_eval\": int(((df[\"label\"] == 0) & ~df[\"is_cal\"]).sum()),\n                      \"stressor_eval\": int(((df[\"label\"] == 1) & ~df[\"is_cal\"]).sum()),\n                      \"calibration_windows\": int(df[\"is_cal\"].sum()),\n                      \"features\": \", \".join(AVAIL[n])} for n, df in WIN.items()])\nsave_table(harm, \"rq3_dataset_harmonisation\")\nprint(harm.to_string(index=False))","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"6e855c15","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 21 · RQ3 within- and cross-dataset experiments ─────────────────────────\ndef make_classifier(name: str):\n    if name == \"logreg\":\n        est = Pipeline([(\"imp\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")), (\"sc\", StandardScaler()),\n                        (\"clf\", LogisticRegression(class_weight=\"balanced\", max_iter=10_000))])\n        return est, {\"clf__C\": list(cfg.logreg_C)}\n    if name == \"hgb\":\n        est = Pipeline([(\"clf\", HistGradientBoostingClassifier(max_iter=cfg.hgb_max_iter, early_stopping=False,\n                                                               class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=cfg.seed))])\n        return est, dict(cfg.hgb_grid)\n    raise ValueError(name)\n\n\ndef youden_threshold(y: np.ndarray, p: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    if np.unique(y).size < 2:\n        return 0.5\n    fpr, tpr, thr = roc_curve(y, p)\n    k = int(np.argmax(tpr - fpr))\n    return float(thr[k]) if np.isfinite(thr[k]) else 0.5\n\n\ndef fit_source(X, y, g, model: str):\n    \"\"\"Tune on source participants (grouped CV), pick the decision threshold from out-of-fold source predictions.\"\"\"\n    est, grid = make_classifier(model)\n    cv = GroupKFold(n_splits=min(cfg.inner_folds, np.unique(g).size))\n    search = GridSearchCV(est, grid, scoring=\"roc_auc\", cv=cv, n_jobs=cfg.n_jobs, refit=True, error_score=np.nan)\n    search.fit(X, y, groups=g)\n    oof = cross_val_predict(clone(search.best_estimator_), X, y, groups=g, cv=cv, method=\"predict_proba\",\n                            n_jobs=cfg.n_jobs)[:, 1]\n    return search.best_estimator_, youden_threshold(y, oof), search.best_params_\n\n\ndef run_within(df: pd.DataFrame, feats: List[str], model: str):\n    X, y, g = df[feats].to_numpy(float), df[\"label\"].to_numpy(int), df[\"subject\"].to_numpy()\n    ev = ~df[\"is_cal\"].to_numpy()\n    p, yhat = np.full(len(df), np.nan), np.full(len(df), -1)\n    for tr, te in GroupKFold(n_splits=min(cfg.outer_folds, np.unique(g).size)).split(X, y, g):\n        est, thr, _ = fit_source(X[tr], y[tr], g[tr], model)\n        te = te[ev[te]]\n        p[te] = est.predict_proba(X[te])[:, 1]\n        yhat[te] = (p[te] >= thr).astype(int)\n    return y[ev], p[ev], yhat[ev], g[ev]\n\n\ndef run_cross(src: pd.DataFrame, tgt: pd.DataFrame, feats: List[str], model: str):\n    est, thr, params = fit_source(src[feats].to_numpy(float), src[\"label\"].to_numpy(int),\n                                  src[\"subject\"].to_numpy(), model)\n    t = tgt[~tgt[\"is_cal\"]]\n    p = est.predict_proba(t[feats].to_numpy(float))[:, 1]\n    return t[\"label\"].to_numpy(int), p, (p >= thr).astype(int), t[\"subject\"].to_numpy()\n\n\ndef cls_metrics(y, p, yhat) -> Dict[str, float]:\n    tn, fp, fn, tp = confusion_matrix(y, yhat, labels=[0, 1]).ravel()\n    both = np.unique(y).size == 2\n    return {\"auroc\": roc_auc_score(y, p) if both else np.nan,\n            \"bacc\": balanced_accuracy_score(y, yhat) if both else np.nan,\n            \"f1_macro\": f1_score(y, yhat, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0),\n            \"sensitivity\": tp / (tp + fn) if (tp + fn) else np.nan,\n            \"specificity\": tn / (tn + fp) if (tn + fp) else np.nan}\n\n\nPRED3 = {}\nnames = list(WIN)\nif len(names) >= 1:\n    with Timer(\"RQ3 transfer experiments\"):\n        for model in cfg.rq3_models:\n            for S in names:\n                for T in names:\n                    feats = [f for f in AVAIL[S] if f in AVAIL[T]]\n                    if not feats:\n                        LOG.warning(f\"RQ3 {S}→{T}: no shared features; skipped\")\n                        continue\n                    for setting in (\"uncalibrated\", \"calibrated\"):\n                        if setting == \"calibrated\" and not (CAN_CAL[S] and CAN_CAL[T]):\n                            continue\n                        src = (WIN if setting == \"uncalibrated\" else WIN_CAL)[S]\n                        tgt = (WIN if setting == \"uncalibrated\" else WIN_CAL)[T]\n                        try:\n                            out = run_within(src, feats, model) if S == T else run_cross(src, tgt, feats, model)\n                            PRED3[(model, S, T, setting)] = (*out, feats)\n                        except Exception as exc:\n                            LOG.warning(f\"RQ3 {model} {S}→{T} [{setting}] failed — {exc}\")\nLOG.info(f\"RQ3 evaluations completed: {len(PRED3)}\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"f73381bd","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 22 · RQ3 subject-cluster bootstrap, paired calibration gain, Figure 5 and S2 ──\ndef cluster_bootstrap(y, g, preds: Dict[str, Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]], n_boot: int, tag: str):\n    \"\"\"Resample participants (clusters) once per replicate and score every prediction set on the same sample.\"\"\"\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(g, return_inverse=True)\n    members = [np.flatnonzero(inv == k) for k in range(uniq.size)]\n    rng = rng_for(tag)\n    res = {k: {\"auroc\": np.full(n_boot, np.nan), \"bacc\": np.full(n_boot, np.nan)} for k in preds}\n    for b in range(n_boot):\n        idx = np.concatenate([members[k] for k in rng.integers(0, uniq.size, uniq.size)])\n        yb = y[idx]\n        if np.unique(yb).size < 2:\n            continue\n        for k, (p, yh) in preds.items():\n            res[k][\"auroc\"][b] = roc_auc_score(yb, p[idx])\n            res[k][\"bacc\"][b] = balanced_accuracy_score(yb, yh[idx])\n    return res\n\n\nrq3_rows = []\nwith Timer(\"RQ3 cluster bootstrap\"):\n    for model in cfg.rq3_models:\n        for S in names:\n            for T in names:\n                ku, kc = (model, S, T, \"uncalibrated\"), (model, S, T, \"calibrated\")\n                sets = {k: PRED3[k] for k in (ku, kc) if k in PRED3}\n                if not sets:\n                    continue\n                y_ref, g_ref = next(iter(sets.values()))[0], next(iter(sets.values()))[3]\n                boot = cluster_bootstrap(y_ref, g_ref, {k[3]: (v[1], v[2]) for k, v in sets.items()},\n                                         cfg.n_boot_cls, f\"rq3_{model}_{S}_{T}\")\n                for k, (y, p, yh, g, feats) in sets.items():\n                    met = cls_metrics(y, p, yh)\n                    a_lo, a_hi = pct_ci(boot[k[3]][\"auroc\"])\n                    b_lo, b_hi = pct_ci(boot[k[3]][\"bacc\"])\n                    row = {\"model\": model, \"source\": S, \"target\": T, \"setting\": k[3],\n                           \"type\": \"within\" if S == T else \"cross\", \"n_target_subjects\": int(np.unique(g).size),\n                           \"n_target_windows\": int(len(y)), \"features\": \", \".join(feats), **met,\n                           \"auroc_ci_low\": a_lo, \"auroc_ci_high\": a_hi, \"bacc_ci_low\": b_lo, \"bacc_ci_high\": b_hi}\n                    if k[3] == \"calibrated\" and \"uncalibrated\" in boot:\n                        gain = boot[\"calibrated\"][\"auroc\"] - boot[\"uncalibrated\"][\"auroc\"]\n                        row[\"auroc_gain\"] = met[\"auroc\"] - cls_metrics(*PRED3[ku][:3])[\"auroc\"]\n                        row[\"auroc_gain_ci_low\"], row[\"auroc_gain_ci_high\"] = pct_ci(gain)\n                    rq3_rows.append(row)\nRQ3_TABLE = pd.DataFrame(rq3_rows)\nif not RQ3_TABLE.empty:\n    within = RQ3_TABLE[RQ3_TABLE[\"type\"] == \"within\"][[\"model\", \"target\", \"setting\", \"auroc\"]].rename(\n        columns={\"auroc\": \"auroc_within_target\"})\n    RQ3_TABLE = RQ3_TABLE.merge(within, on=[\"model\", \"target\", \"setting\"], how=\"left\")\n    RQ3_TABLE[\"auroc_drop_vs_within\"] = RQ3_TABLE[\"auroc_within_target\"] - RQ3_TABLE[\"auroc\"]\n    save_table(RQ3_TABLE, \"rq3_transfer\")\n    RESULTS[\"RQ3\"] = RQ3_TABLE.to_dict(orient=\"records\")\n    print(RQ3_TABLE[[\"model\", \"source\", \"target\", \"setting\", \"auroc\", \"auroc_ci_low\", \"auroc_ci_high\", \"bacc\",\n                     \"auroc_gain\"] if \"auroc_gain\" in RQ3_TABLE else\n                    [\"model\", \"source\", \"target\", \"setting\", \"auroc\", \"bacc\"]].round(3).to_string(index=False))\n\n\ndef transfer_figure(model: str, stem: str, fig_no: str):\n    tab = RQ3_TABLE[RQ3_TABLE[\"model\"] == model]\n    if tab.empty:\n        return\n    settings = [s for s in (\"uncalibrated\", \"calibrated\") if s in set(tab[\"setting\"])]\n    has_gain = \"auroc_gain\" in tab and tab[\"auroc_gain\"].notna().any()\n    ncols = len(settings) + int(has_gain)\n    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(COL2, 2.7), layout=\"constrained\")\n    gs = fig.add_gridspec(1, ncols, width_ratios=[1] * len(settings) + ([1.25] if has_gain else []))\n    cmap = mpl.colormaps[\"cividis\"]\n    axes = []\n    for j, setting in enumerate(settings):\n        ax = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, j])\n        axes.append(ax)\n        M = np.full((len(names), len(names)), np.nan)\n        L = [[\"\" for _ in names] for _ in names]\n        for _, r in tab[tab[\"setting\"] == setting].iterrows():\n            i, k = names.index(r[\"source\"]), names.index(r[\"target\"])\n            M[i, k] = r[\"auroc\"]\n            L[i][k] = f\"{r['auroc']:.2f}\\n[{r['auroc_ci_low']:.2f}–{r['auroc_ci_high']:.2f}]\"\n        im = ax.imshow(M, cmap=cmap, vmin=0.3, vmax=1.0)\n        for i in range(len(names)):\n            for k in range(len(names)):\n                if np.isfinite(M[i, k]):\n                    ax.text(k, i, L[i][k], ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=5.4,\n                            color=\"black\" if M[i, k] > 0.72 else \"white\",\n                            fontweight=\"bold\" if i == k else \"normal\")\n        ax.set_xticks(range(len(names)), names, rotation=30, ha=\"right\")\n        ax.set_yticks(range(len(names)), names if j == 0 else [\"\"] * len(names))\n        ax.set_xlabel(\"Target (test)\")\n        if j == 0:\n            ax.set_ylabel(\"Source (train)\")\n        ax.set_title(setting.capitalize(), loc=\"left\")\n        for sp in ax.spines.values():\n            sp.set_visible(False)\n    cb = fig.colorbar(im, ax=axes, fraction=0.035, pad=0.03)\n    cb.set_label(\"AUROC\", fontsize=6.5)\n    cb.ax.tick_params(labelsize=6)\n    if has_gain:\n        ax = fig.add_subplot(gs[0, ncols - 1])\n        axes.append(ax)\n        gt = tab[tab[\"auroc_gain\"].notna()].reset_index(drop=True)\n        yp = np.arange(len(gt))[::-1]\n        for y_, (_, r) in zip(yp, gt.iterrows()):\n            col = OI[\"grey\"] if r[\"type\"] == \"within\" else OI[\"blue\"]\n            ax.plot([r[\"auroc_gain_ci_low\"], r[\"auroc_gain_ci_high\"]], [y_, y_], color=col, lw=1.0)\n            ax.plot(r[\"auroc_gain\"], y_, \"o\", color=col, ms=3.2)\n        ax.axvline(0, color=\"#777777\", lw=0.6, ls=(0, (3, 2)))\n        ax.set_yticks(yp, [f\"{r['source']}→{r['target']}\" for _, r in gt.iterrows()], fontsize=5.8)\n        ax.set_xlabel(\"ΔAUROC (calibrated − uncalibrated)\")\n        ax.set_title(\"Calibration gain\", loc=\"left\")\n        ax.legend(handles=[Line2D([], [], color=OI[\"blue\"], marker=\"o\", lw=1, ms=3, label=\"cross-dataset\"),\n                           Line2D([], [], color=OI[\"grey\"], marker=\"o\", lw=1, ms=3, label=\"within-dataset\")],\n                  loc=\"best\", fontsize=5.5)\n    label_panels(fig, axes)\n    mname = {\"logreg\": \"L2-logistic regression\", \"hgb\": \"histogram gradient boosting\"}[model]\n    save_fig(fig, stem,\n             f\"Figure {fig_no}. RQ3 ({mname}). AUROC with subject-cluster bootstrap 95% CIs for every source→target pair; \"\n             \"diagonal (bold) = within-dataset grouped cross-validation. Calibrated = baseline-relative features from each \"\n             \"participant's two reserved control windows (excluded from all test sets). Right: paired calibration gain.\")\n\n\nif not RQ3_TABLE.empty:\n    transfer_figure(\"logreg\", \"fig5_rq3_cross_context_transfer\", \"5\")\n    if \"hgb\" in cfg.rq3_models:\n        transfer_figure(\"hgb\", \"figS3_rq3_transfer_gradient_boosting\", \"S3\")\n\n# Figure S2: domain shift before and after calibration\nshift_feats = [f for f in (\"hr_mean\", \"eda_tonic_mean\", \"rmssd_ms\") if any(f in AVAIL[n] for n in names)]\nif shift_feats and names:\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, len(shift_feats), figsize=(COL2, 3.6), squeeze=False, layout=\"constrained\")\n    for j, f in enumerate(shift_feats):\n        for i, (src, title) in enumerate(((WIN, \"raw\"), (WIN_CAL, \"baseline-relative (log-ratio)\"))):\n            ax = axes[i, j]\n            data, labs = [], []\n            for n in names:\n                if n in src and f in AVAIL[n]:\n                    d = src[n][~src[n][\"is_cal\"]]\n                    pair = [d.loc[d[\"label\"] == lab, f].replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan).dropna().to_numpy()\n                            for lab in (0, 1)]\n                    if all(v.size >= 2 for v in pair):          # violinplot cannot draw empty cells\n                        data += pair\n                        labs += [(n, 0), (n, 1)]\n            if not data:\n                ax.axis(\"off\")\n                continue\n            pos = np.arange(len(data)) * 0.9 + np.repeat(np.arange(len(data) // 2) * 0.7, 2)\n            parts = ax.violinplot(data, positions=pos, widths=0.75, showextrema=False, showmedians=True)\n            for body, (n, lab) in zip(parts[\"bodies\"], labs):\n                body.set_facecolor(DATASET_COLOR.get(n, OI[\"grey\"]))\n                body.set_alpha(0.35 if lab == 0 else 0.85)\n                body.set_edgecolor(\"none\")\n            parts[\"cmedians\"].set_color(\"black\")\n            parts[\"cmedians\"].set_linewidth(0.7)\n            centres = pos.reshape(-1, 2).mean(axis=1)\n            ax.set_xticks(centres, [n for n, lab in labs[::2]], fontsize=6)\n            unit = {\"hr_mean\": \"bpm\", \"eda_tonic_mean\": \"µS\", \"rmssd_ms\": \"ms\"}[f]\n            ax.set_ylabel(f\"{FEATURE_LABEL[f]} ({unit})\" if i == 0 else f\"{FEATURE_LABEL[f]} (log-ratio)\")\n            if j == 0:\n                ax.set_title(title.capitalize(), loc=\"left\")\n    handles = [Patch(facecolor=OI[\"grey\"], alpha=0.35, label=\"control\"),\n               Patch(facecolor=OI[\"grey\"], alpha=0.85, label=\"stressor\")]\n    try:\n        fig.legend(handles=handles, loc=\"outside upper right\", ncol=2, fontsize=6.5)   # matplotlib ≥ 3.7\n    except ValueError:\n        fig.legend(handles=handles, loc=\"upper right\", ncol=2, fontsize=6.5)\n    save_fig(fig, \"figS2_domain_shift\",\n             \"Figure S2. Distribution of harmonised features by dataset and condition (light = control, dark = stressor) \"\n             \"before (top) and after (bottom) personal-baseline calibration. Medians shown as horizontal lines.\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"5a0151be","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## RQ4 (exploratory) — Does recovery burden align with self-reported resilience?\nCD-RISC measures *trait* psychological resilience; recovery burden is a *state* response to one task. They are not\nexpected to be equivalent constructs, so this is a convergent-validity check, not a validation of either measure.","metadata":{}},{"id":"17b92753","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 23 · RQ4 Spearman correlation and Figure 6 ─────────────────────────────\nd4 = PART[[\"subject\", \"RB_comp\", \"cdrisc\"]].dropna()\nif len(d4) >= 8:\n    rho, p_rho = stats.spearmanr(d4[\"RB_comp\"], d4[\"cdrisc\"])\n    rng = rng_for(\"rq4_boot\")\n    bs = np.full(cfg.n_boot, np.nan)\n    a, b = d4[\"RB_comp\"].to_numpy(), d4[\"cdrisc\"].to_numpy()\n    for i in range(cfg.n_boot):\n        idx = rng.integers(0, len(a), len(a))\n        if np.ptp(a[idx]) > 0 and np.ptp(b[idx]) > 0:\n            bs[i] = stats.spearmanr(a[idx], b[idx])[0]\n    lo, hi = pct_ci(bs)\n    RESULTS[\"RQ4\"] = {\"n\": int(len(d4)), \"spearman_rho\": float(rho), \"ci\": [lo, hi], \"p\": float(p_rho)}\n    save_table(pd.DataFrame([{\"n\": len(d4), \"spearman_rho\": rho, \"ci_low\": lo, \"ci_high\": hi, \"p\": p_rho}]),\n               \"rq4_resilience\")\n    LOG.info(f\"RQ4 (n={len(d4)}): Spearman ρ = {fmt_ci(rho, lo, hi)}, {fmt_p(p_rho)}\")\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(COL1, 2.5), layout=\"constrained\")\n    ax.scatter(d4[\"cdrisc\"], d4[\"RB_comp\"], s=13, color=OI[\"blue\"], alpha=0.85, lw=0)\n    sl, ic, _, _ = stats.theilslopes(d4[\"RB_comp\"], d4[\"cdrisc\"])\n    gx = np.linspace(d4[\"cdrisc\"].min(), d4[\"cdrisc\"].max(), 50)\n    ax.plot(gx, ic + sl * gx, color=OI[\"vermillion\"], lw=1.0, label=\"Theil–Sen fit\")\n    ax.set_xlabel(\"CD-RISC-10 score\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Recovery burden (mean |z|, R1)\")\n    ax.text(0.97, 0.97, f\"Spearman ρ = {rho:.2f} [{lo:.2f}, {hi:.2f}]\\n{fmt_p(p_rho)}, n = {len(d4)}\",\n            transform=ax.transAxes, ha=\"right\", va=\"top\", fontsize=6.5)\n    ax.set_ylim(top=d4[\"RB_comp\"].max() * 1.22)\n    save_fig(fig, \"fig6_rq4_resilience\",\n             \"Figure 6. RQ4 (exploratory). Composite recovery burden versus self-reported resilience (CD-RISC-10). \"\n             \"Line: Theil–Sen fit. Bracket: participant-bootstrap 95% CI.\")\nelse:\n    LOG.warning(\"RQ4 skipped: fewer than 8 participants with both measures\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"9c7a2244","cell_type":"code","source":"# ── 24 · Results summary, figure manifest and reproducibility record ───────\nRESULTS[\"figures\"] = FIGURES\nRESULTS[\"data_sources\"] = {\"physionet\": f\"{PN_ROOT} [{PN_SOURCE}]\", \"wesad_subjects\": [p.stem for p in WESAD_PKLS],\n                           \"swell_files\": [p.name for p in SWELL_CSVS], \"swell_has_subject_ids\": SWELL_HAS_SUBJECTS}\nwith open(OUT / \"results_summary.json\", \"w\") as fh:\n    json.dump(RESULTS, fh, indent=2, default=lambda o: o.item() if hasattr(o, \"item\") else str(o))\npd.DataFrame(FIGURES).to_csv(OUT / \"figure_manifest.csv\", index=False)\n\nprint(\"=\" * 88)\nprint(\"RESULTS SUMMARY\")\nprint(\"=\" * 88)\nif \"RQ1\" in RESULTS:\n    r = RESULTS[\"RQ1\"]\n    print(f\"RQ1  n={r['n']}: standardised β(recovery burden) = {fmt_ci(r['beta_RB'], *r['ci_HC3'])} \"\n          f\"[HC3], {fmt_p(r['p_HC3'])}; bootstrap 95% CI [{r['ci_bootstrap'][0]:.2f}, {r['ci_bootstrap'][1]:.2f}]\")\nif \"RQ2\" in RESULTS:\n    for row in RESULTS[\"RQ2\"][\"table\"]:\n        print(f\"RQ2  {row['learner']:<18} MAE A = {row['MAE_A']:.1f}  B = {row['MAE_B']:.1f}  \"\n              f\"ΔMAE = {fmt_ci(row['dMAE_A_minus_B'], row['dMAE_ci_low'], row['dMAE_ci_high'], 1)}  \"\n              f\"R²oos A = {row['R2oos_A']:.2f}  B = {row['R2oos_B']:.2f}\")\n    print(f\"     Ridge permutation p (one-sided) = {RESULTS['RQ2']['ridge_permutation_p_one_sided']:.4f}\")\nif not RQ3_TABLE.empty:\n    for _, r in RQ3_TABLE[RQ3_TABLE[\"model\"] == \"logreg\"].iterrows():\n        g = (f\"  gain {fmt_ci(r['auroc_gain'], r['auroc_gain_ci_low'], r['auroc_gain_ci_high'])}\"\n             if \"auroc_gain\" in r and np.isfinite(r.get(\"auroc_gain\", np.nan)) else \"\")\n        print(f\"RQ3  {r['source']:>9} → {r['target']:<9} [{r['setting']:<12}] AUROC \"\n              f\"{fmt_ci(r['auroc'], r['auroc_ci_low'], r['auroc_ci_high'])}{g}\")\nif \"RQ4\" in RESULTS:\n    r = RESULTS[\"RQ4\"]\n    print(f\"RQ4  n={r['n']}: Spearman ρ = {fmt_ci(r['spearman_rho'], *r['ci'])}, {fmt_p(r['p'])}\")\nprint(\"-\" * 88)\nprint(f\"Outputs: {OUT.resolve()}\")\nfor f in FIGURES:\n    print(f\"  {f['stem']:<45} {f['files']}\")","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"4ac53dba","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Reading the results responsibly\n* **Sample size.** RQ1/RQ2 rest on ≈ 35 participants. Report effect sizes with their intervals; a non-significant\n  recovery coefficient is *imprecision*, not evidence of no association.\n* **Fixed order.** Stress 2 always follows Recovery 1, so practice, fatigue and habituation are confounded with time.\n  RQ1 is associational; RQ2 shows predictive utility, not mechanism.\n* **Physiological specificity.** EDA and HR also change with movement, posture and temperature. The motion-filtered\n  sensitivity analysis addresses only part of this.\n* **Transportability ≠ deployment.** RQ3 positives are experimental stressor *conditions*. Cross-dataset stress\n  detection with WESAD and SWELL-KW has been studied before, so RQ3 is supporting evidence, not the novelty claim.\n* **Before claiming novelty,** review prior work on recovery dynamics and repeated stress (e.g. the dataset authors'\n  own work on recurrent task-induced stress) and state precisely what this analysis adds.\n\n**Cite:** Roy & Nuamah (2026) PhysioNet doi:10.13026/x3vc-p627 · Goldberger/Pollard et al. PhysioNet ·\nSchmidt et al. (2018) WESAD, ICMI · Koldijk et al. (2014) SWELL-KW, ICMI.","metadata":{}}]}